## What it is

A story-driven, open-world role-playing game set in the futuristic streets of Night City.

## Is this your kind of game?

Consider this if character development and a story set in a futuristic city are what you want from an evening of play. Watch an ordinary gameplay sequence to see the balance between conversations, travel, and combat.

## Download and purchase

This is a paid game. Check the official store for current regional pricing, editions, and purchase terms. Use the official Steam button on this page to open the publisher's listing. Installation is handled by Steam; GameNews does not host installers or game files.

Compare the base game and any expansion or bundle carefully. Use the requirements for the content you actually intend to buy rather than an old release-day specification.

## What the Steam listing shows

Checked 23 November 2026. Steam lists CD PROJEKT RED as both developer and publisher, with a release date of 9 December 2020. Steam files it as a single-player RPG with full controller support and Steam Cloud saves. Expansions and other add-ons are listed separately from the base game.

The minimum column asks for 64-bit Windows 10, a Core i7-6700 or Ryzen 5 1600, 12 GB of memory, a GeForce GTX 1060 6GB, Radeon RX 580 8GB, or Arc A380, DirectX 12, and 70 GB of storage. Steam says an SSD is required. The listing also carries a photosensitivity warning about visual effects that may cause seizures in a minority of people.

Steam’s content notice says the game contains strong language, intense violence, blood and gore, and nudity and sexual material.

## Sources and editorial basis

Product information checked against the [official Steam listing](https://store.steampowered.com/app/1091500/?l=english) on 16 October 2026 and rechecked on 23 November 2026. Selected with reference to [Steam's most-played chart](https://store.steampowered.com/charts/mostplayed/). This is a researched profile, not a hands-on review or a search-volume ranking. Live prices, player counts, and performance scores are intentionally not quoted.
